// The ambient world actors -- LEGO Loco's townspeople/animals and its road traffic.
//
// Two leaf classes over one shared base, distinguished purely by the TileKind CATEGORY of the
// kind id they were spawned from (`TileKind::TileKind_GetCategory(kindId)`, 0x446030, which is
// just `(kindId >> 10) & 0xff` -- see docs/TILEKIND_IDS.md, generated by tools/resstrings.py):
//
//   category 7  (ids 0x1c00-0x1fff)  people\* + animals\*   -> WalkerActor      (0xf4 bytes)
//   category 8  (ids 0x2000-0x23ff)  vehicles\*             -> RoadVehicleActor (0xf0 bytes)
//
// The single factory is DecorObjMgrMaybe::SpawnActorForKindMaybe (0x4349d0), which branches on
// that category and returns 0 for every other one. Both are spawned by a placed building
// (FUN_00458430) from its kind descriptor's own 5-entry candidate table
// (BigObj::aPossibleMinifigs, +0x524 -- src/CursorDesc.h), under a global population cap
// of nActiveCategory7Maybe + nActiveCategory8Maybe < 100.
//
// ⚠ These were catalogued for many sessions as `NetMsgPayload7`/`NetMsgPayload8`, "clone wire
// records into per-participant/roster objects". That was REFUTED end-to-end in v388 -- nothing
// in either class touches the network stack -- and the classes were renamed to
// DecorActor7Maybe/DecorActor8Maybe, then to their present certain names in v389 once the
// resource-string table pinned the two categories to `people\`/`animals\` and `vehicles\`.
// Do not confuse the old name with GameNetMsgQueue.h's `NetMsgPayloadObjMaybe`, which is a
// DIFFERENT and still-valid (still unidentified) model of the queue's 0xe/0x10 payload case.
//
// Behaviour, shared by both leaves: pick a destination (nDestPos), resolve it to a tile on the
// actor's own network (paths\* / category 0xc for WalkerActor, roads\* / category 0xd for
// RoadVehicleActor), then step toward it one tile at a time, re-deciding at
// dwNextDecisionTickMaybe. WalkerActor additionally boards trains -- pRidingTrainMaybe -- which
// is the ONLY reason it is allowed onto a category-3 (track\*) tile.
#pragma once

#include "WidgetBase.h"   // AnimDescRefObj0x477488 -- the shared base at offset 0
#include "TilePlacedObj.h"

class PeerTrainNode;
struct PeerTrainNodePartial; // src/PeerTrainNode.h -- the real, modeled train node (same
                              // object as the never-defined `PeerTrainNode` handle type)
class TrackGraph;            // src/TrackGraph.h

// 0xf0/240 bytes; ctor 0x433a20, dtor 0x433be0, vtable 0x477f18 (22 slots: 15 inherited from
